      and he found it dated. Now the first screen is a centred, confident H1 in
      white with the site's italic accent, the same two buttons, and a band of
      large photographs running underneath on their own.

      The H1 is the live copy, unchanged; only the layout moved. The small line
      above it is sentence case, not an eyebrow: the page has none now.

      THE STRIP is the client logo band's technique (clients.css): two
      identical runs side by side, translated by exactly half, so the loop is
      seamless. It pauses on hover, and with reduced motion it stops and
      becomes a plain sideways scroll. It is scenery under the heading, so it
      is aria-hidden. No vans: the van livery still shows the old number. #}
