    {# ===================== 2b — TRUSTED BY =====================
      THE REAL BAND, NOT A HAND-BUILT ROW. What stood here was six typed words
      in dashed boxes, slots held until artwork arrived. The client artwork
      arrived in 0cbb6c9 and every other page has shown the marks since; this
      page, the one that matters most, was the last still showing text. Rather
      than drop the files into the old row, this is the component the service
      pages and /gallery/ already use: nine marks, monochrome, moving.

      ON PAPER, not light. .hp-intro above is section--light, and two pale
      sections running together read as one long one.

      THE "ACCREDITED BY" ROW IS NOT HERE. It was CHAS and UKAS as two more
      dashed text boxes, and there is still no artwork for either. Both claims
      are made in words in CREDENTIALS below ("CHAS accredited" and
      "UKAS-accredited laboratory testing"), so nothing is lost by waiting.
      When the marks land they want their own small row, not this marquee: an
      accreditation is not a client.
    #}
    {% set clientsId = "home-clients" %}
    {% set clientsTitle = "Trusted by" %}
    {% set clientsClass = "clients--compact" %}
    {% set clientsSurface = "section--light" %}
    {% include "clients.njk" %}

    {# ===================== 3 — SERVICES =====================
      ONE HEADING, THEN THE CARDS (Matt, 14/10/26: "to get to the services,
      there's a lot of copy"). The page ran a separate problem section, a
      47-word paragraph, a hairline and "What do you need to sort?" before the
      first card. Now one short heading introduces the four routes; the cards
      below are already the questions the visitor arrives with.

      ROUTED BY PROBLEM, NOT LISTED BY SERVICE. Every heading here is the
      question the visitor arrived with, because someone who has just been
      served a notice does not search for "water hygiene", they search for what
      has gone wrong. The service name is on the page they land on.

      Set as an asymmetric ruled spread rather than a card grid: five equal
      tiles would say these are five equivalent choices, and they are not.
    #}
    <section class="section hp-services" id="services" aria-labelledby="hp-services-title">
      <div class="container">
        {# "From borehole to tap, the services we offer" (Matt, 14/10/26): the
           customer's phrase, then a plain label for what the cards are. The problem line
           that headed this read as a warning, not a way into four services.
           This is the Elstead client's own phrase ("from the borehole pump
           right through to the taps"), and it spans every card below, from the
