               until Matt vetoed it, 14/10/26.) Same script as the home hero (hero-media.js), on a slower
               hold so the two never change together. Only the first frame
               carries alt text: the others are the same story told again, and
               inside a link a screen reader would read all three. With no JS
               or with reduced motion, the first frame simply stays. #}
            <span class="hp-svc__media parallax" data-crossfade data-crossfade-hold="7000">
              <img class="is-active" src="/assets/b-estate-7931.webp" alt="A mini digger on the lawn of a timber-framed country house, with a borehole pump and hose laid out on the grass." width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
              <img src="/assets/r-cottage-2765.webp" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
              <img src="/assets/lk-effingham-8608.webp" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            </span>
            {# Matt's wording (14/10/26). People weighing this up think "a
